# PR opened — agent checklist (DocCy)

When the user says they opened / created / pushed a PR (or asks to watch CI on a new PR), do this **in chat** every time. Do **not** rely on GitHub PR description checkboxes for these reminders — the user reads those too late.

## 1. Local register gate (not CI) — run it yourself

Immediately start the testing-DB register E2E (do **not** wait for the user to ask):

```bash
npm run test:e2e:register
```

Live `/register` (Places/Auth/Resend), founder email asserted, doctor deleted afterwards. See `docs/ci-test-policy.md`.

In the same turn, **tell the user** that you launched it and that you will report the result when it finishes. Stay on the run until it completes (pass/fail); if it fails, diagnose and fix (or report clearly if blocked).

Do **not** only remind them to run it themselves. Do **not** ask permission first.

Do **not** add this block back into PR body templates as the primary reminder path.

## 2. Watch CI and fix failures

Stay on the PR checks **while the PR stays open**. Report status in chat (not only in a background terminal). If any fail, diagnose and fix (push to the PR branch). Prefer fixing real product/test mismatches over blind re-runs.

## 3. Master / coworker sync (Livio) — ongoing

Coworker: **Livio** (`elance1985`, typically `liviolanzo@gmail.com`).

This is not a one-shot at PR open. **While the PR remains open** (and especially while watching CI), periodically `git fetch origin master` and check whether this branch is behind `origin/master`.

- If behind: report it in chat immediately, list the missing commits, and **call out Livio’s commits explicitly** when present.
- Ask before merging/rebasing `master` into the PR branch unless the user already asked to update from master.
- Do not assume “we checked once at open” is enough — a coworker merge can land while CI is still running.
